# prom_b/exports.syms -- the prom_b labels prom_a references (GENERATED, scripts/tools/join_maincpu_link.py)
#
# The Makefile runs `llvm-objcopy --globalize-symbols=prom_b/exports.syms` on wsa1_prom_b.llvm.o
# before the joint link (maincpu/maincpu.ld), so prom_a's undefined references to these names
# resolve to prom_b's labels.  Every other label stays local.  Why a file and not `.global` in
# the source: a global label is a relocation, and llvm-mc relaxes a short branch to it to the
# long form, which changes the bytes (scripts/tools/join_maincpu_link.py docstring).
# A label renamed in prom_b and not here leaves prom_a's reference undefined: the link fails.

